    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a net release of GBP 25.4m from prior year reserves in 2022, primarily due to more favourable claims development than originally anticipated. This release partially offset adverse developments from prior years, including GBP 8.2m in natural catastrophe losses, a GBP 7.6m deterioration in COVID-19 loss estimates, and GBP 4.6m from the South Africa Riots large loss, all from 2021. Earlier years also saw significant impacts from COVID-19 losses (GBP 152.7m in 2020), natural catastrophes like Derecho storms and Hurricane Laura (GBP 18.4m in 2020), and California Wildfires, Hurricane Florence, and Hurricane Michael (GBP 22.8m in 2018). The 2019 year was also impacted by higher than expected losses on prior years of account.",
